    "body": "Sure, those will be good things to work on/get automatically when we update IDL. But they're orthogonal to this.\r\n\r\nI'm eager to hear more from implementers on whether postMessaging within a process should always share or should sometimes copy. (For that matter, we still need to decide what postMessaging across a process does---the discussion in #936 is assuming some kind of error, but maybe just copying is fine.)",
